        "location_url": "https://data.cdc.gov/d/ivdz-qhnr",
        "description": "Immunization Information Systems (IIS) are the confidential, population-based registries that states, some large cities, and territories use to record vaccine doses given by participating providers. Jurisdictions submit counts to CDC each month, by age group, of residents with at least one dose of flu vaccine, RSV vaccine among adults 75 and older, or RSV monoclonal antibody among infants under 8 months. Counts are cumulative from the start of the season and are divided by the previous year's Census population estimate to give coverage. Completeness varies with each jurisdiction's reporting laws and provider participation, so IIS coverage usually runs below survey estimates. Fifty-four jurisdictions reported through the 2024-25 season and about half as many in 2025-26, and CDC publishes no national estimate.",
